{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1785260962,"nonce":"q7RlO0vhi2v77N7c2fiOz5X1XXw=","title":"ADR-0062: the stat-cache capture instant is not persisted, so a Depot restart degrades the re-ingest drain to \"trust nothing\"","message":"The `(size, mtime, ctime)` stat cache is only sound against a capture instant stamped **at least 1 ms after** materialisation completed (ADR-0062's measured contract). `ExportRecord.prepared_at` is whole **seconds** and is stamped **before** the copy, so it cannot serve.\n\n`workspaced.rs` therefore captures the millisecond instant in `WorkspaceState` after `prepare` returns. A Depot restart forgets it and the drain degrades to a capture of `0` — every file re-read, nothing reused. Safe and logged, but it silently loses the entire point of the baseline for every in-flight Export.\n\n- [ ] A millisecond capture instant persisted in the Export record (bump `RECORD_VERSION`; an older record honestly has none)\n- [ ] A restart mid-Export keeps the baseline useful\n- [ ] Assert the degraded path is still *correct* (capture 0 ⇒ rehash everything), so the fallback stays safe rather than merely rare","files":null}]}